s\u202f1\u20134 we have:\n\n* The minimum possible number of sunny lines is \\(\\displaystyle k_{\\min}= \\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil\\).\n* Every integer \\(k\\) with \\(k_{\\min}\\le k\\le n\\) can be realised.\n* In particular, \\(k=0\\) is also attainable (Lemma\u202f1), which coincides with the formula for \\(k_{\\min}\\) when \\(n=3,4\\).\n\nHence the set of admissible values of \\(k\\) is exactly  \n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\left\\{\\,\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil,\\;\n\\Bigl\\lceil\\frac{n-2}{2}\\Bigr\\rceil+1,\\dots ,n\\right\\}} .\n\\]"
