athcal T_n\\;\\Big|\\;b\\ge n-k\\Bigr\\}.\n   \\]\n\n   For a point of \\(\\mathcal I_n\\) we have  \n\n   \\[\n   a\\le n+1-b\\le n+1-(n-k)=k+1 .\n   \\]\n\n   Hence \\(a\\) can take the values \\(1,2,\\dots ,k+1\\).  \n   The points with \\(a=1\\) are already covered by the vertical line \\(x=1\\).  \n   For each \\(a\\in\\{2,3,\\dots ,k+1\\}\\) there is exactly one admissible \\(b\\), namely  \n\n   \\[\n   b=n+1-a .\n   \\]\n\n   Consequently \\(\\mathcal I_n\\) contains precisely the \\(k\\) points  \n\n   \\[\n   P_i=(i+1,\\;n-i)\\qquad (i=0,1,\\dots ,k-1).\n   \\tag{3}\n   \\]\n\n   Choose \\(k\\) pairwise distinct slopes \\(m_0,m_1,\\dots ,m_{k-1}\\) such that  \n\n   \\[\n   m_i\\notin\\{0,\\infty,-1\\}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad m_i\\neq m_j\\;(i\\neq j).\n   \\]\n\n   For each \\(i\\) define the sunny line  \n\n   \\[\n   \\ell_i:\\; y=m_i x +\\bigl(n-i-m_i(i+1)\\bigr).\n   \\tag{4}\n   \\]\n\n   By construction \\(\\ell_i\\) passes through the point \\(P_i\\) and is sunny.  \n   Because the slopes are distinct, the lines \\(\\ell_i\\) are distinct and none coincides with any of the previously chosen horizontal or vertical lines.\n\n   *Verification of coverage.*  \n   - If a point \\((a,b)\\in\\mathcal T_n\\) satisfies \\(b\\le n-k-1\\), then it lies on the horizontal line \\(y=b\\).  \n   - If \\(b\\ge n-k\\) and \\(a=1\\), it lies on the vertical line \\(x=1\\).  \n   - If \\(b\\ge n-k\\) and \\(a\\ge 2\\), then \\((a,b)\\) is one of the points \\(P_i\\) in (3) and therefore lies on the sunny line \\(\\ell_i\\).  \n\n   Hence every lattice point of \\(\\mathcal T_n\\) is covered by at least one of the \\(n\\) constructed lines.\n\n   *Adjustment for smaller \\(k\\).*  \n   When \\(k<n-2\\) we already have exactly \\(n\\) lines (the \\(n-k\\) non\u2011sunny ones plus the \\(k\\) sunny ones).  \n   If we wish to increase the number of non\u2011sunny lines while keeping the same \\(k\\), we may replace some of the horizontal lines \\(y=2,\\dots ,y=n-k-1\\) by